  era: "c. 2600\u20131900 BCE \xB7 Section 2 \xB7 Indus Valley Civilisation \xB7 c. 3300 \u2013 1300 BCE (mature phase c. 2600 \u2013 1900 BCE)"
  title: Town planning
  text: Harappan cities were laid out on a grid, with main streets crossing at right angles. Many had a raised, walled citadel and a larger lower town. Houses opened onto side lanes, and standard bricks in the ratio one to two to four were used everywhere.
